butes natural gas in Idaho, Minnesota, Montana, North Dakota, Oregon, South Dakota, Washington, and Wyoming through approximately 22,000 miles of distribution and 540 miles transmission systems; and supplies related value-added services. In addition, it provides natural gas transportation and underground storage services through a regulated pipeline system primarily in the Rocky Mountain and northern Great Plains regions; and cathodic protection non-regulated energy-related services. Further, the company offers transportation and storage services. MDU Resources Group, Inc. was incorporated in 1924 and is headquartered in Bismarck, North Dakota.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Nicole A. Kivisto | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $895K ranks in the below the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["MDU Resources Group, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $3.9B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -35% over the past three years and -8% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $297M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 69% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6862554532113448},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Utilities peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 56/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Utilities peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is MDU Resources Group (MDU) Still Reasonably Priced For Dividend Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-mdu/mdu-resources-group/news/is-mdu-resources-group-mdu-still-reasonably-priced-for-divid","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793965186.388,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.799,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"MDU Resources Reports Q3 2026 Results with 213.4M Shares Outstanding","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/mdu-resources-reports-q3-2026-results-with-2134m-shares-outstanding","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793964233.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MDU Resources (MDU) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/mdu-resources-mdu-q3-2026-225003720.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793919003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.19,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MDU reaffirms $0.93-$1 2026 EPS while advancing $2.8B-$3.1B Bakken East pipeline (NYSE:MDU)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667422-mdu-reaffirms-0_93-1-2026-eps-while-advancing-2_8b-3_1b-bakken-east-pipeline","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793915372.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MDU Resources Gr Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/62943871/mdu-resources-gr-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793906841.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MDU Q3 Earnings Miss Estimates on Higher Costs, Revenues Rise Y/Y","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024791/mdu-q3-ea